⚡ Quick Recovery Cheat Sheet
Linksys E4200v2 / EA4500 (Viper) – Fast Serial Flash Procedure
This is the minimal, fastest possible sequence to bring a soft‑bricked E4200v2/EA4500 back to life and booting OpenWrt.

🔌 1. Connect Serial
115200 baud, 8N1

Pins: GND – TX – RX (3.3V logic)

Open terminal before powering the router

🟢 2. Power On & Interrupt U‑Boot
You must see:

Code
Hit any key to stop autoboot:
Press any key → get:

Code
Viper>>
If no serial output → cold boot again (unplug → wait → plug in).
If still nothing → see Troubleshooting Appendix.

🌐 3. Set TFTP Environment
Code
setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.10
setenv serverip 192.168.1.2
PC must be 192.168.1.2 with TFTP running.

📥 4. Load Firmware Into RAM
Code
tftpboot 0x800000 ea4500.bin
Note the hex size at the end, e.g.:

Code
Bytes transferred = 8912896 (880000 hex)
🧹 5. Erase Firmware Region
Code
nand erase 0x200000 0x1e00000
💾 6. Write Firmware to NAND
Use the size from the TFTP output:

Code
nand write 0x800000 0x200000 0x880000
🔄 7. DO NOT TRUST reset — Power Cycle Instead
Typing:

Code
reset
will freeze the router (solid LED, no boot).
This is normal.

Correct action:
Unplug power

Wait 5–10 seconds

Plug power back in

🚀 8. Router Boots Into OpenWrt
You should now see:

Code
Starting kernel ...
Default access:

IP: 192.168.1.1

User: root

Password: (none)

🟩 Done — Recovery Successful
